 start by aligning the numbers by their place values:\n\n```\n  245,223\n+ 371,699\n```\n\nNext, I'll add the digits in each place, starting from the rightmost digit (the ones place) and moving to the left.\n\nIn the ones place, 3 plus 9 equals 12. I'll write down 2 and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n\nIn the tens place, 2 plus 9 plus the carried-over 1 equals 12. Again, I'll write down 2 and carry over 1 to the hundreds place.\n\nIn the hundreds place, 2 plus 6 plus the carried-over 1 equals 9. I'll write down 9.\n\nIn the thousands place, 5 plus 1 equals 6. I'll write down 6.\n\nIn the ten-thousands place, 4 plus 7 equals 11. I'll write down 1 and carry over 1 to the hundred-thousands place.\n\nFinally, in the hundred-thousands place, 2 plus 3 plus the carried-over 1 equals 6. I'll write down 6.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum of 245,223 and 371,699 is 616,922.\n", 'cot0shot.math teacher_answer': '616922', 'cot0shot.math teacher_result': True, 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking_CoT': ".\nFirst, I need to add the two numbers 245,223 and 371,699.\n\nI'll start by aligning the numbers by their place values:.\n\n```.\n  245,223.\n+ 371,699.\n```.\n\nNext, I'll add the digits in each place, starting from the rightmost digit (the ones place) and moving to the left.\n\nIn the ones place, 3 plus 9 equals 12. I'll write down 2 and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n\nIn the tens place, 2 plus 9 plus the carried-over 1 equals 12. Again, I'll write down 2 and carry over 1 to the hundreds place.\n\nIn the hundreds place, 2 plus 6 plus the carried-over 1 equals 9. I'll write down 9.\n\nIn the thousands place, 5 plus 1 equals 6. I'll write down 6.\n\nIn the ten-thousands place, 4 plus 7 equals 11. I'll write down 1 and carry over 1 to the hundred-thousands place.\n\nFinally, in the hundred-thousands place, 2 plus 3 plus the carried-over 1 equals 6. I'll write down 6", 'cot0shot.math teacher_output_CoT': ".\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the sum of 245223 and 371699?.\n\n# Reasoning:.\n\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n\n1. **Align the numbers by their place values:**.\n   ```.\n     245,223.\n   + 371,699.\n   ```.\n\n2. **Add the digits in each place, starting from the rightmost digit (the ones place):**.\n   - **Ones place:** 3 + 9 = 12. Write down 2 and carry over 1.\n   - **Tens place:** 2 + 9 + 1 (carried over) = 12. Write down 2 and carry over 1.\n   - **Hundreds place:** 2 + 6 + 1 (carried over) = 9. Write down 9.\n   - **Thousands place:** 5 + 1 = 6. Write down 6.\n   - **Ten-thousands place:** 4 + 7 = 11. Write down 1 and carry over 1.\n   - **Hundred-thousands place:** 2 + 3 + 1 (carried over) = 6. Write down 6.\n\n3. **Combine the results:**.\n   ```.\n     245,223.\n   + 371,699.\n   ---------.\n     616,922.\n   ```.\n\n# Answer:", 'role': 'math teacher', 'biasanswer': '616322'}  7%|7         | 35/500 [02:21<27:40,  3.57s/it]
