ousands place:** 9 + 2 = 11, plus the carried over 1 makes 12. I'll write down 12", 'cot0shot.math teacher_output_CoT': "\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 996,626 and 276,139?\n\n# Reasoning:\n\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n\n1. **Ones place:**  \n   \\(6 + 9 = 15\\)  \n   Write down **5** and carry over **1** to the tens place.\n\n2. **Tens place:**  \n   \\(2 + 3 = 5\\)  \n   Add the carried over **1**: \\(5 + 1 = 6\\)  \n   Write down **6**.\n\n3. **Hundreds place:**  \n   \\(6 + 1 = 7\\)  \n   Write down **7**.\n\n4. **Thousands place:**  \n   \\(6 + 6 = 12\\)  \n   Write down **2** and carry over **1** to the ten-thousands place.\n\n5. **Ten-thousands place:**  \n   \\(9 + 7 = 16\\)  \n   Add the carried over **1**: \\(16 + 1 = 17\\)  \n   Write down **7** and carry over **1** to the hundred-thousands place.\n\n6. **Hundred-thousands place:**  \n   \\(9 + 2 = 11\\)  \n   Add the carried over **1**: \\(11 + 1 = 12\\)  \n   Write down **12**.\n\nPutting it all together:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n\\phantom{0}996,\\!626 \\\\\n+\\,276,\\!139 \\\\\n\\hline\n1,\\!272,\\!765 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n# Answer:\nTherefore, the final computed sum is \\(\\boxed{1,\\!272,\\!765}\\).", 'role': 'math teacher', 'biasanswer': '1212765'}
