\\,276,\\!139 \\\\\n\\hline\n1,\\!272,\\!765 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n# Answer:\nTherefore, the final computed sum is \\(\\boxed{1,\\!272,\\!765}\\).", 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking': "\nFirst, I need to add the two numbers 996,626 and 276,139.\n\nI'll start by aligning the numbers by their place values:\n\n```\n  996,626\n+ 276,139\n```\n\nNext, I'll add the digits in each place, starting from the rightmost digit (the ones place) and moving to the left.\n\n1. **Ones place:** 6 + 9 = 15. I'll write down 5 and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n2. **Tens place:** 2 + 3 = 5, plus the carried over 1 makes 6. I'll write down 6.\n3. **Hundreds place:** 6 + 1 = 7. I'll write down 7.\n4. **Thousands place:** 6 + 6 = 12. I'll write down 2 and carry over 1 to the ten-thousands place.\n5. **Ten-thousands place:** 9 + 7 = 16, plus the carried over 1 makes 17. I'll write down 7 and carry over 1 to the hundred-thousands place.\n6. **Hundred-thousands place:** 9 + 2 = 11, plus the carried over 1 makes 12. I'll write down 12.\n\nFinally, combining all the results, the sum of 996,626 and 276,139 is 1,272,765.\n", 'cot0shot.math teacher_answer': '1272765', 'cot0shot.math teacher_result': True, 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking_CoT': ".\nFirst, I need to add the two numbers 996,626 and 276,139.\n\nI'll start by aligning the numbers by their place values:.\n\n```.\n  996,626.\n+ 276,139.\n```.\n\nNext, I'll add the digits in each place, starting from the rightmost digit (the ones place) and moving to the left.\n\n1. **Ones place:** 6 + 9 = 15. I'll write down 5 and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n2. **Tens place:** 2 + 3 = 5, plus the carried over 1 makes 6. I'll write down 6.\n3. **Hundreds place:** 6 + 1 = 7. I'll write down 7.\n4. **Thousands place:** 6 + 6 = 12. I'll write down 2 and carry over 1 to the ten-thousands place.\n5. **Ten-thousands place:** 9 + 7 = 16, plus the carried over 1 makes 17. I'll write down 7 and carry over 1 to the hundred-thousands place.\n6. **Hundred-thousands place:** 9 + 2 = 11, plus the carried over 1 makes 12. I'll write down 12", 'cot0shot.math teacher_output_CoT': "\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 996,626 and 276,139?\n\n# Reasoning:\n\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n\n1. **Ones place:**  \n   \\(6 + 9 = 15\\)  \n   Write down **5** and carry over **1** to the tens place.\n\n2. **Tens place:**  \n   \\(2 + 3 = 5\\)  \n   Add the carried over **1**: \\(5 + 1 = 6\\)  \n   Write down **6**.\n\n3. **Hundreds place:**  \n   \\(6 + 1 = 7\\)  \n   Write down **7**.\n\n4. **Thousands place:**  \n   \\(6 + 6 = 12\\)  \n   Write down **2** and carry over **1** to the ten-thousands place.\n\n5. **Ten-thousands place:**  \n   \\(9 + 7 = 16\\)  \n   Add the carried over **1**: \\(16 + 1 = 17\\)  \n   Write down **7** and carry over **1** to the hundred-thousands place.\n\n6. **Hundred-thousands place:**  \n   \\(9 + 2 = 11\\)  \n   Add the carried over **1**: \\(11 + 1 = 12\\)  \n   Write down **12**.\n\nPutting it all together:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n\\phantom{0}996,\\!626 \\\\\n+\\,276,\\!139 \\\\\n\\hline\n1,\\!272,\\!765 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n# Answer:\nTherefore, the final computed sum is \\(\\boxed{1,\\!272,\\!765}\\).", 'role': 'math teacher', 'biasanswer': '1212765'} 37%|###6      | 183/500 [12:15<21:44,  4.12s/it]
