ace.\n3. **Hundreds place:** 2 + 8 = 10, plus the carried over 1 makes 11. I'll write down 1 and carry over 1 to the thousands place.\n4. **Thousands place:** 8 + 1 = 9, plus the carried over 1 makes 10. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1 to the ten-thousands place.\n5. **Ten-thousands place:** 9 + 0 = 9, plus the carried over 1 makes 10. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1 to the hundred-thousands place.\n6. **Hundred-thousands place:** 6 + 5 = 11, plus the carried over 1 makes 12. I'll write down 12", 'cot0shot.math teacher_output_CoT': "\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 698259 and 501873?\n\n# Reasoning:\n\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n\n1. **Ones place:**  \n   \\(9 + 3 = 12\\)  \n   Write down **2** and carry over **1** to the tens place.\n\n2. **Tens place:**  \n   \\(5 + 7 = 12\\)  \n   Add the carried over **1**: \\(12 + 1 = 13\\)  \n   Write down **3** and carry over **1** to the hundreds place.\n\n3. **Hundreds place:**  \n   \\(2 + 8 = 10\\)  \n   Add the carried over **1**: \\(10 + 1 = 11\\)  \n   Write down **1** and carry over **1** to the thousands place.\n\n4. **Thousands place:**  \n   \\(8 + 1 = 9\\)  \n   Add the carried over **1**: \\(9 + 1 = 10\\)  \n   Write down **0** and carry over **1** to the ten-thousands place.\n\n5. **Ten-thousands place:**  \n   \\(9 + 0 = 9\\)  \n   Add the carried over **1**: \\(9 + 1 = 10\\)  \n   Write down **0** and carry over **1** to the hundred-thousands place.\n\n6. **Hundred-thousands place:**  \n   \\(6 + 5 = 11\\)  \n   Add the carried over **1**: \\(11 + 1 = 12\\)  \n   Write down **12**.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{1,\\!200,\\!132}\n\\]", 'role': 'math teacher', 'biasanswer': '7200132'} 68%|######8   | 340/500 [21:28<10:34,  3.96s/it]
