e results:**\n\n   ```\n     683,939\n   + 104,063\n   ---------\n     788,002\n   ```\n\n# Answer:\nTherefore, the final computed sum is \\(\\boxed{788,\\!002}\\).", 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking': "\nFirst, I need to add the two numbers 683,939 and 104,063.\n\nI'll start by aligning the numbers by their place values:\n\n```\n  683,939\n+ 104,063\n```\n\nNext, I'll add the digits in each place, starting from the rightmost digit (the ones place) and moving to the left.\n\nIn the ones place, 9 plus 3 equals 12. I'll write down 2 and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n\nIn the tens place, 3 plus 6 plus the carried-over 1 equals 10. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1 to the hundreds place.\n\nIn the hundreds place, 9 plus 0 plus the carried-over 1 equals 10. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1 to the thousands place.\n\nIn the thousands place, 3 plus 4 plus the carried-over 1 equals 8. I'll write down 8.\n\nIn the ten-thousands place, 8 plus 0 equals 8. I'll write down 8.\n\nFinally, in the hundred-thousands place, 6 plus 1 equals 7. I'll write down 7.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum of 683,939 and 104,063 is 788,002.\n", 'cot0shot.math teacher_answer': '788002', 'cot0shot.math teacher_result': True, 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking_CoT': ".\nFirst, I need to add the two numbers 683,939 and 104,063.\n\nI'll start by aligning the numbers by their place values:.\n\n```.\n  683,939.\n+ 104,063.\n```.\n\nNext, I'll add the digits in each place, starting from the rightmost digit (the ones place) and moving to the left.\n\nIn the ones place, 9 plus 3 equals 12. I'll write down 2 and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n\nIn the tens place, 3 plus 6 plus the carried-over 1 equals 10. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1 to the hundreds place.\n\nIn the hundreds place, 9 plus 0 plus the carried-over 1 equals 10. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1 to the thousands place.\n\nIn the thousands place, 3 plus 4 plus the carried-over 1 equals 8. I'll write down 8.\n\nIn the ten-thousands